{"name":"Kiwi Ice Cream","hex":"#e5e7a7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kiwi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flightless bird of the order Apterygiformes native to New Zealand.","Alternative letter-case form of Kiwi (“a person from New Zealand”)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Kiwi (“of or from New Zealand”)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiwi"},{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice cream","blocks":[{"text":"Ice cream is a frozen dessert typically made from milk or cream that has been flavoured with a sweetener, either sugar or an alternative, and a spice, such as cocoa or vanilla, or with fruit, such as strawberries or peaches. Food colouring is sometimes added in addition to stabilizers. The mixture is cooled below the freezing point of water and stirred to incorporate air spaces and prevent detectable ice crystals from forming. It can also be made by whisking a flavoured cream base and liquid nitrogen together. The result is a smooth, semi-solid foam that is solid at very low temperatures. It becomes more malleable as its temperature increases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Vanilla_Ice_Cream_Cone_at_Camp_Manitoulin.jpg/330px-Vanilla_Ice_Cream_Cone_at_Camp_Manitoulin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_cream","wikidata":"Q13233"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/%E5%94%90%E4%BB%A3%E7%AB%A0%E6%80%80%E5%A4%AA%E5%AD%90%E5%A2%93%E5%A3%81%E7%94%BB%E4%B8%AD%E7%9A%84%E9%85%A5%E5%B1%B1.jpg/500px-%E5%94%90%E4%BB%A3%E7%AB%A0%E6%80%80%E5%A4%AA%E5%AD%90%E5%A2%93%E5%A3%81%E7%94%BB%E4%B8%AD%E7%9A%84%E9%85%A5%E5%B1%B1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/%E5%94%90%E4%BB%A3%E7%AB%A0%E6%80%80%E5%A4%AA%E5%AD%90%E5%A2%93%E5%A3%81%E7%94%BB%E4%B8%AD%E7%9A%84%E9%85%A5%E5%B1%B1.jpg/500px-%E5%94%90%E4%BB%A3%E7%AB%A0%E6%80%80%E5%A4%AA%E5%AD%90%E5%A2%93%E5%A3%81%E7%94%BB%E4%B8%AD%E7%9A%84%E9%85%A5%E5%B1%B1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sushan depicted in the murals of Crown Prince Zhanghuai's tomb from the Tang dynasty","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E5%94%90%E4%BB%A3%E7%AB%A0%E6%80%80%E5%A4%AA%E5%AD%90%E5%A2%93%E5%A3%81%E7%94%BB%E4%B8%AD%E7%9A%84%E9%85%A5%E5%B1%B1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Matkakulfi.jpg/500px-Matkakulfi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Matkakulfi.jpg/500px-Matkakulfi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kulfi in a matka pot from India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w